# Vitest/Jest snapshots are machine-generated serializations of rendered output.
# They legitimately contain trailing whitespace (e.g. JSX " and " text nodes that
# serialize as a standalone " and " line), so exempt them from git's whitespace
# checks — otherwise `git diff --check` / `git apply` flag every regenerated
# snapshot as a corrupt patch. The fix is per the snapshot class, not per file.
*.snap -whitespace
